Dear Rahul,

You can use something like:

X "--X " c (FALSE, TRUE)
Y "--Y " c  (FALSE, TRUE)
Z "--Z " c  (FALSE, TRUE)

A1 "--A " r (0,10) |X ==  "FALSE"
B1 "--B " r (0,10) |Y ==  "FALSE"
C1 "--C " r (0,10) |Z ==  "FALSE"
A2 "--A " r (0,100) |X ==  "TRUE"
B2 "--B " r (0,100) |Y ==   "TRUE"
C2 "--C " r (0,100) |Z ==   "TRUE"
WEIGHT  "--w "         c              (0.0005)

Since irace will not change the parameter WEIGHT, it doesn't matter that the type is categorical.

Cheers,

Manuel.

