irace (or any automatic algorithm configuration method) is designed to find good parameter settings given a set of training problem instances. My guess is that nobody had tried to run irace without any instances. So, "it worked out" by sheer luck and I'm not even sure that you can expect anything useful from the results. I'm sure there are many ways to provide invalid inputs to irace and make it crash or do nonsense. We try to detect those cases and provide nice error messages but obviously we haven't thought about all possible invalid inputs.

I tried various ways of not providing instances for version 3.0, and everything I have tried gives a clear error already with "--check" and without.

Cheers,

Manuel.

